From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] LuaIDE/WatchesPanel: LUA_NUMTAGS compat for Lua 5.5

Sibling fix to Patch0010 (lua_newstate signature). Lua 5.5 dropped
the `LUA_NUMTAGS` public macro; it had been retained in 5.4 as a
deprecation-alias for `LUA_NUMTYPES` in `lua.h`. Engine code in
`Code/Tools/LuaIDE/Source/LUA/WatchesPanel.cpp` references
`LUA_NUMTAGS` at two sites (lines 834 + 838 -- the `c > LUA_NUMTAGS`
bounds check and the `static_assert` checking the typeStringLUT size
matches the type-tag count). Both fail to compile on Lua 5.5+.

Caught on COPR build 10437498 (o3de-experimental, fedora-rawhide
chroot, 2026-05-08): the build progressed past the ScriptContext.cpp
site (covered by Patch0010) only to fail later at the LuaIDE compile
with `error: use of undeclared identifier 'LUA_NUMTAGS'`. Patch0010
was load-bearing but incomplete.

Approach: add a one-line compat shim right after `<AzCore/Script/lua/
lua.h>` is included. On Lua 5.5+ define `LUA_NUMTAGS` as an alias for
the still-present `LUA_NUMTYPES` (which has the same semantic value).
On Lua 5.4 the `#if` branch evaluates false and the engine's existing
references to `LUA_NUMTAGS` (which lua.h provides as the upstream
alias) compile unchanged.

This is sibling to Patch0010 in the same way they're both Lua 5.5
compat fixes, but they target different files and different API
surfaces (call-site signature drift vs. removed compat macro). Worth
pitching upstream alongside Patch0010 once the patch shape settles
across both -- benefits every distro on the rawhide Lua 5.5
trajectory (Fedora 45+, Debian unstable, Alpine edge, Arch).

Caveat: there may be MORE Lua 5.5 break sites in the engine that we
haven't tripped on yet because they live in even-later-built source
files. The right way to find them all is `grep -rn LUA_NUMTAGS Code/
Gems/` against the engine source on a CS10/F45-class lua-devel-5.5
sysroot. Phase 2 work; not blocking this fix.

Memory note: project_lua_5_5_newstate_break.md (existing) updated
to reference this patch as the second-of-N Lua 5.5 compat fixes.

Signed-off-by: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
---
--- a/Code/Tools/LuaIDE/Source/LUA/WatchesPanel.cpp
+++ b/Code/Tools/LuaIDE/Source/LUA/WatchesPanel.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,12 @@
 #include "LUAEditorDebuggerMessages.h"
 #include <AzCore/Casting/numeric_cast.h>
 #include <AzCore/Script/lua/lua.h>
+
+// Lua 5.5 dropped the LUA_NUMTAGS public macro that 5.4 retained as a
+// deprecation-alias for LUA_NUMTYPES. Restore the alias on 5.5+ so the
+// existing call sites below compile unchanged. Behavior-preserving on 5.4.
+#if LUA_VERSION_NUM >= 505 && !defined(LUA_NUMTAGS)
+#  define LUA_NUMTAGS LUA_NUMTYPES
+#endif
+
 #include <Source/LUA/moc_WatchesPanel.cpp>

 #include <QSortFilterProxyModel>
